contentText:
This March, Jimmy Hession , an artist manager at Milk & Honey, was ironing out a producer agreement with the Sony-owned, European dance label B1 Recordings for his client Paul Harris , who worked on the Alok and Khalid track “Dive into Me.” When Sony Music Germany sent over the deal terms, Hession discovered some novel language: a broad release allowing the use of Harris’ work for AI training. &nbsp;

